    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-viii">Alfonso VIII</a> marched to Alarcos without waiting for the reinforcements coming from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-ix-of-leon">Alfonso IX of León</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sancho-vii-of-navarre">Sancho VII of Navarre</a>.</li><li>The Castilian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heavy-cavalry">heavy cavalry</a> broke the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> front lines and killed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a>, but the Arab left enveloped its flank and rear and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaqub-al-mansur">al-Mansur</a>'s rearguard then attacked.</li><li>The victory proved short-lived: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaqub-al-mansur">al-Mansur</a> went back to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> in 1198, and his successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-al-nasir">Muhammad al-Nasir</a> was defeated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-las-navas-de-tolosa">Las Navas de Tolosa</a> in 1212.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Pedro Fernández de Castro, who held a personal feud against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-viii">Alfonso</a>, rode with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a> and was sent by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> to negotiate the surrender of the castle of Alarcos.</p></aside>
    </section>

